Here are a few ways to write a Rust function that removes duplicates from a `Vec<T>`, depending on the type of elements in the vector.

The most idiomatic and efficient way to remove duplicates is usually by using a `HashSet`.

### 1. Using `HashSet` (Recommended for most types)

This approach leverages the properties of a `HashSet` (which only stores unique elements) to filter the original vector.

```rust
use std::collections::HashSet;

